\chapter{Simulation Engine Architecture}

\section{Overview}
The Matter Jet Mk-30 relies on a sovereign computational architecture capable of
executing relativistic magnetohydrodynamic (RMHD) simulations, real-time
telemetry ingestion, cryptographic verification, and safety interlock logic at
petawatt-scale energy throughput. This chapter develops the numerical methods,
GPU parallelization strategies, cryptographic pipelines, and stability criteria
governing the Mk-30 simulation engine.

\section{Relativistic MHD Simulation Kernel}
The RMHD equations solved by the Mk-30 simulation engine are:
\begin{align}
\partial_t \rho + \nabla \cdot (\rho \mathbf{v}) &= 0, \\
\rho \left( \partial_t \mathbf{v} + (\mathbf{v} \cdot \nabla)\mathbf{v} \right)
&= -\nabla p + \mathbf{J} \times \mathbf{B}, \\
\partial_t \mathbf{B} &= \nabla \times (\mathbf{v} \times \mathbf{B}), \\
\nabla \cdot \mathbf{B} &= 0.
\end{align}

The simulation kernel evolves:
\begin{itemize}
\item density $\rho$,
\item velocity $\mathbf{v}$,
\item magnetic field $\mathbf{B}$,
\item pressure $p$,
\item current density $\mathbf{J}$.
\end{itemize}

\section{Finite Volume Method}
The Mk-30 employs a finite volume method (FVM) with:
\begin{itemize}
\item second-order spatial reconstruction,
\item relativistic Riemann solvers,
\item divergence-free magnetic field enforcement.
\end{itemize}

The conserved variables are:
\begin{equation}
\mathbf{U} =
\begin{pmatrix}
\rho \\
\rho \mathbf{v} \\
\mathbf{B} \\
E
\end{pmatrix},
\end{equation}
where $E$ is total energy density.

\section{Runge-Kutta Time Integration}
Time evolution uses a fourth-order Runge-Kutta (RK4) scheme:
\begin{align}
\mathbf{U}_1 &= \mathbf{U}^n + \Delta t\, \mathbf{F}(\mathbf{U}^n), \\
\mathbf{U}_2 &= \mathbf{U}^n + \frac{\Delta t}{2}\, \mathbf{F}(\mathbf{U}_1), \\
\mathbf{U}_3 &= \mathbf{U}^n + \frac{\Delta t}{2}\, \mathbf{F}(\mathbf{U}_2), \\
\mathbf{U}_4 &= \mathbf{U}^n + \Delta t\, \mathbf{F}(\mathbf{U}_3), \\
\mathbf{U}^{n+1} &= \frac{1}{6}(\mathbf{U}_1 + 2\mathbf{U}_2 + 2\mathbf{U}_3 + \mathbf{U}_4).
\end{align}

